==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|de|Waben|g=m||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|wabe}}, from {{inh|de|goh|waba|g1=f}}, {{m|goh|wabo|g2=m}}, from the root of {{m|de|weben|t=to weave}}. Originally restricted to [[Upper German]], standardized in the 18th century. A [[Central German]] synonym was {{m|de|Roß}} ({{m+|gmh|rāz}}), compare {{noncog|nl|raat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈvaːbə/}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-Wabe.ogg|a=Austria}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f}}

# {{lb|de|often|in the plural}} [[honeycomb]]

====Usage notes====
* The singular refers to a sheet of honeycomb in [[apiarian]] parlance, in layman’s use and figuratively also to a single cell:
:: {{uxi|de|Jede '''Wabe''' besteht aus sechseckigen Zellen.|Every '''honeycomb''' is made up of hexagonal cells.}}
:: {{uxi|de|Jede '''Wabe''' ist sechseckig.|Every '''honeycomb cell''' is hexagonal.}}

